{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773756674,"nonce":"+hKuaLo+sUB8UnqxwcTa5SVl/QE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM7zto3k","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/2","origin":"github"},"title":"Document IzzyBoat network setup as reference for BizzyBoat configuration","message":"## Summary\n\nDocument IzzyBoat's (EchoBoat 160) complete network configuration to serve as the reference design for BizzyBoat (EchoBoat 240). This documentation should capture all networking details so we can design a compatible multi-boat setup.\n\n## Motivation\n\nWe are setting up BizzyBoat (Big IzzyBoat), a new EchoBoat 240, to work alongside our existing EchoBoat 160, IzzyBoat. Before designing BizzyBoat's network config, we need a clear, consolidated reference of IzzyBoat's current network architecture.\n\n## Details to Document\n\n### UDP Bridge Configuration\n- **Robot side**: name `izzy`, port `4200`, max packet size 1000\n- **Operator side**: name `operator`, remote `izzy`\n- **Connections**: `wifi` and `vpn` with distinct bandwidth limits\n  - WiFi: 1.5 MB/s max, VPN: 1.0 MB/s max\n- **Hostnames**: `mystique_ib` (robot wifi), `salmon_ib` (operator wifi), `mystique_v` (robot VPN), `salmon_v` (operator VPN)\n- **Topic bridging**: full topic list for wifi vs. reduced set for VPN\n\n### Network Interfaces \u0026 Hostnames\n- Robot computer hostname conventions (e.g., `mystique` with `_ib`/`_v` suffixes)\n- Operator computer hostname conventions (e.g., `salmon` with `_ib`/`_v` suffixes)\n- Host entries or DNS setup required\n\n### ROS 2 Networking\n- `ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=LOCALHOST` (per `start_tmux_project11.bash`)\n- Namespace: `izzy`, frame prefix: `izzy/`\n- Operator namespace: `operator`\n\n### Sensor Network\n- Norbit sonar IP: `192.168.53.34`\n- FCU (ArduPilot) serial: `/dev/ttyUSB0:57600`\n- GCS URL: `udp://@192.168.12.8`\n\n### NTRIP RTK Corrections\n- Host: `macorsrtk.massdot.state.ma.us:31000`\n- Mountpoint: `RTCM3_MASA`\n- RTCM routed to `mavros/gps_rtk/send_rtcm`\n\n### External Services\n- Foxglove bridge (operator side)\n- ROS TCP endpoint (Unity, operator side)\n\n## Deliverable\n\nA `docs/network_setup.md` (or similar) in this repo documenting all of the above, with enough detail that BizzyBoat's network config can be designed to coexist on the same operator station without conflicts (e.g., distinct namespaces, ports, hostnames).\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n- `izzyboat_project11/config/izzyboat.yaml` — robot-side UDP bridge, sensor, and logger config\n- `izzyboat_project11/config/operator.yaml` — operator-side UDP bridge config\n- `izzyboat_project11/launch/izzyboat_launch.py` — main robot launch\n- `izzyboat_project11/launch/operator_core_launch.py` — operator launch\n- `izzyboat_project11/launch/ntrip_launch.py` — NTRIP RTK setup\n- `izzyboat_project11/scripts/start_tmux_project11.bash` — autostart script with ROS env vars\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}